<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.1.1: Understanding a Situation with Quadratic Equations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02086</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.1.1: Understanding a Situation with Quadratic Equations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>cadf6774-1650-427d-b6be-927e7ca2d615</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up</title>
      <para id="para-00001">A mechanical device is used to launch a potato vertically into the air. The potato is launched from a platform 20 feet above the ground, with an initial vertical velocity of 92 feet per second.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">The function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>92</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> models the height of the potato over the ground, in feet, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> seconds after launch.</para>
      <para id="para-00003">Here is the graph representing the function.</para>
      <para id="para-00004">
          <media alt="A graph showing height in feet versus time in seconds; the curve rises, peaks at 4 seconds and 160 feet, then descends, crossing the x axis at 6 seconds.">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_09_03_02_01.svg"/>
          </media>
        
     </para>
      <para id="para-00005">For each question, explain your reasoning.</para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00006">What is the height of the potato 1 second after launch?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00007">Enter the height of the potato 1 second after launch.</para>
          <para id="para-00008">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00009">The height of the potato 1 second after launch will be 96 feet. Substituting 1 second into the function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> yields:</para>
          <para id="para-00010"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:msup><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>92</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>92</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>96</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00011">Will the potato still be in the air 8 seconds after launch?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00013">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00014">No, from the graph, we can see the potato will land before 8 seconds after the launch.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00015">Will the potato reach 120 feet? If so, when will it happen?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00017">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00018">Yes, from the graph, we can see the potato’s height will be 120 feet at two times: approximately 1.5 seconds and 4.3 seconds after launch.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00019">When will the potato hit the ground, or have a height of zero feet?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          
          <para id="para-00021">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00022">We can see from the graph the potato will hit the ground, or have a height of zero feet, after approximately 6 seconds.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
